.TH ENVCTL 1 "2026" "envctl 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
envctl \- manage named shell environments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B envctl
[\fIGLOBAL OPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
envctl manages named environments: profiles capturing shell variables, PATH
entries, aliases, functions, and an optional working directory. Profiles are
stored as TOML under XDG directories and applied to the current shell by
emitting shell code for \fBeval\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize the config directory and defaults.
.TP
.B add, create \fINAME\fR
Create a new environment.
.TP
.B remove, delete \fINAMES...\fR
Delete environments (confirmation, backup, --force, --dry-run).
.TP
.B edit \fINAME\fR
Edit via $EDITOR or flags (--set, --unset, ...).
.TP
.B view, show \fINAME\fR
Show an environment.
.TP
.B list, ls
List environments with filtering/sorting/paging.
.TP
.B set \fINAME KEY VALUE\fR
Set a variable (KEY=VALUE also accepted).
.TP
.B unset \fINAME KEYS...\fR
Remove variables.
.TP
.B rename, mv \fIOLD NEW\fR
Rename an environment.
.TP
.B clone, cp \fISRC DST\fR
Duplicate an environment.
.TP
.B import \fIFILE|-\fR
Import from .env/JSON/YAML/TOML.
.TP
.B export \fINAME\fR
Export to stdout or file.
.TP
.B diff \fIA B\fR
Compare two environments.
.TP
.B validate [NAMES...]
Validate environments.
.TP
.B activate, use \fINAME\fR
Emit shell code to activate.
.TP
.B deactivate
Emit shell code to restore previous state.
.TP
.B which, current
Show the active environment.
.TP
.B completion \fIbash|zsh|fish\fR
Generate shell completions.
.TP
.B secret set|get|rm|list
Manage secrets in the system keyring.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Config file path.
.TP
.B \-\-profile \fINAME\fR
Named config profile.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Verbose logging.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Quiet mode.
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Assume yes.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print actions without applying.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable color.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIFMT\fR
table|json|yaml|plain.
.TP
.B \-\-no-input
Non-interactive mode.
.TP
.B \-\-system
System-wide store (requires root).
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Debug logging.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 generic error, 2 usage error, 3 not found, 4 permission denied.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/envctl
Config directory.
.TP
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/envctl
State directory (active snapshot, backups, lock).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
Used to detect target shell for activate.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Used by edit.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME
XDG base directories.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
envctl init
.TP
envctl add work --var FOO=bar --path-prepend /opt/bin
.TP
eval "$(envctl activate work)"
.TP
envctl export work --format json
.SH SEE ALSO
bash(1), zsh(1), fish(1)
